1. Container image (Dockerfile, built in your AWS account by AWS CodeBuild)

Base image: python:3.12.15-slim from public.ecr.aws/docker/library/python, pinned by digest. Python is under the
PSF License Agreement (https://docs.python.org/3/license.html) and pip (which the Dockerfile upgrades to 26.2.2,
uses to install the packages, then removes) under the MIT License; the Debian packages in the image are under their
own licenses (https://www.debian.org/legal/licenses/).

Python packages that the Dockerfile installs: torch 2.14.1 (CPU build), strands-decider 0.2.0, transformers
5.20.2, strands-agents 1.62.0, mcp 1.30.0 and boto3, with the dependencies they resolved to on 25 October 2026
(Python 3.12). Dependency versions can differ when you build. To list them for your own image, run
pip-licenses --with-urls inside it.

Each entry gives the package, its version, its license as declared in the package metadata, and its URL.

